\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the policies by acceptance regime: mean over the 24 instances (seeds averaged within each instance) and standard error. $F_{\text  {Gini}}$ is the Gini coefficient of hourly earnings over the eligible couriers (connected $\ge 1$ h, idle ones at zero), ``active eligible'' the share of eligible couriers that delivered at least one order, and $F_{\text  {Gini}}^{\text  {act}}$ the Gini coefficient over all the couriers who delivered at least one order, including those connected for less than one hour. $F_{\text  {Deficit}}$ is the share of active couriers below $w^*$. Payment is relative to the flat tariff of the orders delivered. \textbf  {Greedy-Arrival} is from the review experiment, on the same ten seeds as X1\relax }}{22}{table.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:benchmark}{{2}{22}{Comparison of the policies by acceptance regime: mean over the 24 instances (seeds averaged within each instance) and standard error. $\FG $ is the Gini coefficient of hourly earnings over the eligible couriers (connected $\ge 1$ h, idle ones at zero), ``active eligible'' the share of eligible couriers that delivered at least one order, and $\FGa $ the Gini coefficient over all the couriers who delivered at least one order, including those connected for less than one hour. $\FD $ is the share of active couriers below $w^*$. Payment is relative to the flat tariff of the orders delivered. \textbf {Greedy-Arrival} is from the review experiment, on the same ten seeds as X1\relax }{table.caption.19}{}}
